# Component rules

Applies to everything in `src/components/`. The root conventions still apply.

## Data in, markup out

- Components receive amounts as `MinorUnits` and render them with `formatMinor`.
  A component never does arithmetic on a price itself, and never receives a
  pre formatted string where a number belongs.
- No data fetching inside a component. Call `apiClient` from the page or an action
  and pass the result down as props.

## Props and types

- Props are a named exported interface with explicit types. No `any`, no index
  signatures standing in for a real shape.
- Optional props get a default at the destructuring site, not a `!` later on.

## Markup

- Tailwind utility classes only, no inline `style` objects and no new CSS files.
- Interactive elements are real `button` or `a` elements with an accessible label,
  never a `div` with an `onClick`.
- User facing copy lives in the component that renders it. Keep it in sentence
  case and avoid exclamation marks.
